NanoPi NEO3 onboard fan connector (CON4, 2-pin JST ZH 1.5mm, 5V).
CON4 is switched from VDD_5V by an AO3415A P-FET driven via a 2N7002
from RK3328 PWM2 / GPIO2_A6 (schematic sheet 11, "FAN"), so PWM duty
controls fan speed. The PWM must be slow (100 Hz): the P-FET gate
recharges through 100k pull-ups (~70us), so at high PWM frequencies
the FET never switches off and any duty behaves like full speed.
Registers a pwm-fan cooling device on the SoC thermal zone with a
continuous 50% baseline above 40C (off below 35C), stepping through
59/69/78/89/100% at 54/58/62/66/70C. The always-on baseline keeps
the SoC temperature steady instead of on/off cycling around the
lowest trip point.
